(5825209, 848346, 98339, '<td valign="top">for me this is to processed...but I will say such a wonderful beast to capture</td>', 'for me this is to processed...but I will say such a wonderful beast to capture', '2010-01-22 22:19:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5825210, 848625, 105441, '<td valign="top">Excellent.  A surprising use of B&amp;W, beautifully executed.  9</td>', 'Excellent.  A surprising use of B&W, beautifully executed.  9', '2010-01-22 22:20:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5825211, 848482, 98977, '<td valign="top">Sacrificing a little sleep to get up and shoot this one seems worth it to me.  Beautiful color. Classic subject matter. I get the feeling that I might want to see a similar shot from a little bit different angle.</td>', 'Sacrificing a little sleep to get up and shoot this one seems worth it to me.  Beautiful color. Classic subject matter. I get the feeling that I might want to see a similar shot from a little bit different angle.', '2010-01-22 22:20:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5825212, 848647, 43463, '<td valign="top">There is an explosion of lines/shapes and color here in this composition. While beautiful and verdant the tight bunching of so many lines and extra vibrant color makes it all the harder for the eye to drink in the scene. I am sure that a large size print of 16 x 20 it would look great large scale but when you translate it down to small scale it just hits the eye all at once and becomes overwhelming. One thing that bothers me is that the extra vibrant violet colors of the floral floor. It looks too saturated. While I see some wonderful shadows and midtones in the trunks of the trees to define each individual shape, I don''t quite see the same mimicked in the flowers. It''s there but not to the same degree - and I wonder if that selection was less saturated and had a boost in the shadows/midtones if it would ground and define the scene more.</td>', 'There is an explosion of lines/shapes and color here in this composition. While beautiful and verdant the tight bunching of so many lines and extra vibrant color makes it all the harder for the eye to drink in the scene. I am sure that a large size print of 16 x 20 it would look great large scale but when you translate it down to small scale it just hits the eye all at once and becomes overwhelming. One thing that bothers me is that the extra vibrant violet colors of the floral floor. It looks too saturated. While I see some wonderful shadows and midtones in the trunks of the trees to define each individual shape, I don''t quite see the same mimicked in the flowers. It''s there but not to the same degree - and I wonder if that selection was less saturated and had a boost in the shadows/midtones if it would ground and define the scene more.', '2010-01-22 22:20:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5825213, 848835, 38032, '<td valign="top">nice subtle HDR and comp.</td>', 'nice subtle HDR and comp.', '2010-01-22 22:20:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5825214, 847147, 98339, '<td valign="top">this is really pretty, but I''m wondering if you ran USM on this?  It seems that if you pumped that up a bit more it would really define the ice patches.</td>', 'this is really pretty, but I''m wondering if you ran USM on this?  It seems that if you pumped that up a bit more it would really define the ice patches.', '2010-01-22 22:21:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5825215, 848341, 98339, '<td valign="top">for me this is a bit soft in the focus...but a very beautiful girl</td>', 'for me this is a bit soft in the focus...but a very beautiful girl', '2010-01-22 22:21:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5825217, 848562, 98339, '<td valign="top">sorry but this isn''t enough to hold my interest...it''s not a bad picture...just not a wow picture..</td>', 'sorry but this isn''t enough to hold my interest...it''s not a bad picture...just not a wow picture..', '2010-01-22 22:21:36.000000', NULL, 1),
