(5838934, 848830, 2333, '<td valign="top">One of my top picks of the challenge. A stunning scene, obviously, but also very well executed, and processed very nicely on the whole. My only slight niggle is the stars, which seem oversharpened. I find that this happens on downsizing with bicubic sharper when the larger image is already quite sharp. I sometimes find that this type of image needs a little different treatment when resizing for web. <br/>You chose well on exposure, capturing detail in the auroras, as well as getting nice exposure on the foreground. It so easy to over-do these shots in post-processing, and you have avoided that; you''ve showed how it *should* be done.<br/>Normally clouds detract from a scene like this, but in this case they are just a beautiful addition!</td>', 'One of my top picks of the challenge. A stunning scene, obviously, but also very well executed, and processed very nicely on the whole. My only slight niggle is the stars, which seem oversharpened. I find that this happens on downsizing with bicubic sharper when the larger image is already quite sharp. I sometimes find that this type of image needs a little different treatment when resizing for web. You chose well on exposure, capturing detail in the auroras, as well as getting nice exposure on the foreground. It so easy to over-do these shots in post-processing, and you have avoided that; you''ve showed how it *should* be done.Normally clouds detract from a scene like this, but in this case they are just a beautiful addition!', '2010-01-27 21:07:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5838936, 848507, 79955, '<td valign="top">You did a good job on the exposure. The background is distracting and the overall appeal to the viewer is lacking IMO , 5</td>', 'You did a good job on the exposure. The background is distracting and the overall appeal to the viewer is lacking IMO , 5', '2010-01-27 21:08:25.000000', NULL, 1),
