(5842696, 848788, 100773, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Deen:</b></div><hr/><i> Damn, 2 photos, 2 ribbons, you are really a monster!<br/> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Nah, he''s not a monster... He''s from Iceland. Icelandic people win ribbons even without submitting =)<br/> <br/>But I''m sure glad you did, because this is fantastic photo you have shared with us!</td>', 'Originally posted by Deen: Damn, 2 photos, 2 ribbons, you are really a monster!   Nah, he''s not a monster... He''s from Iceland. Icelandic people win ribbons even without submitting =) But I''m sure glad you did, because this is fantastic photo you have shared with us!', '2010-01-29 04:16:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5842700, 848725, 110041, '<td valign="top">One thing I learnt quickly on dpc is to know your audience. There are styles of photography that are favoured and so trying something a little quirky or ''different'' is bound to be slated by some - and their entitled to do that, so there''s no point getting a sulk on.<br/> <br/>For me, as long as I''m enjoying photography, I don''t mind if nobody ''gets'' what I''ve done, but it is great when someone does, and it only takes one person. Of course it might be completely different for you, but keep going regardless.<br/> <br/>For what it''s worth, my initial reaction was similar to the majority who said "out of focus" etc. But having spent time and read a bit more about what you were trying to achieve, it puts the photo in a whole different light. So well done.</td>', 'One thing I learnt quickly on dpc is to know your audience. There are styles of photography that are favoured and so trying something a little quirky or ''different'' is bound to be slated by some - and their entitled to do that, so there''s no point getting a sulk on. For me, as long as I''m enjoying photography, I don''t mind if nobody ''gets'' what I''ve done, but it is great when someone does, and it only takes one person. Of course it might be completely different for you, but keep going regardless. For what it''s worth, my initial reaction was similar to the majority who said "out of focus" etc. But having spent time and read a bit more about what you were trying to achieve, it puts the photo in a whole different light. So well done.', '2010-01-29 04:25:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5842715, 847104, 36606, '<td valign="top">very pretty. tunning vibrant shot.</td>', 'very pretty. tunning vibrant shot.', '2010-01-29 04:57:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5842716, 848273, 43463, '<td valign="top">Just saw this in the posted Outtakes what it looked like before - Wha!!!???? I can''t figure out why this placed so far down? Fabulous job in PP as I said before this is a fabulous travel shot that looks like it could appear in a travel brochure - I certainly enjoyed the beauty of the place shown in the shot ( I am one of your 8''s). Hmmmm, maybe the reason it placed low is because of monitor calibration - others might have seen it as too dark? (I hate varying calibrations because you never know *exactly* how others are going to see it)</td>', 'Just saw this in the posted Outtakes what it looked like before - Wha!!!???? I can''t figure out why this placed so far down? Fabulous job in PP as I said before this is a fabulous travel shot that looks like it could appear in a travel brochure - I certainly enjoyed the beauty of the place shown in the shot ( I am one of your 8''s). Hmmmm, maybe the reason it placed low is because of monitor calibration - others might have seen it as too dark? (I hate varying calibrations because you never know *exactly* how others are going to see it)', '2010-01-29 04:57:47.000000', NULL, 0),
