(5843509, 847762, 30861, '<td valign="top">I figured this has to be you, and I was right :-) One of my 10''s. Faceless feets, faithful rendering, and the arrow just makes the image, a grace note <i>par excellence</i>. Ridiculously low score, my sympathies.</td>', 'I figured this has to be you, and I was right :-) One of my 10''s. Faceless feets, faithful rendering, and the arrow just makes the image, a grace note par excellence. Ridiculously low score, my sympathies.', '2010-01-29 14:18:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5843510, 847833, 103032, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jdannels:</b></div><hr/><i> I thought this would break a 6. I like it. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks, I appreciate it.<br/>And thanks again to everyone who left comments.  I especially got a chuckle from <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=37845" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">VitaminB</a>''s comment.  I admire and get inspired by all the photographers here on DPC who have great vision, creativity, and great PP skills.  As as an average photographer who lacks PP skills, this is a great site to learn.<br/>Have a great day.</td>', 'Originally posted by jdannels: I thought this would break a 6. I like it.  Thanks, I appreciate it.And thanks again to everyone who left comments.  I especially got a chuckle from  VitaminB''s comment.  I admire and get inspired by all the photographers here on DPC who have great vision, creativity, and great PP skills.  As as an average photographer who lacks PP skills, this is a great site to learn.Have a great day.', '2010-01-29 14:19:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5843512, 848800, 30861, '<td valign="top">An 8 from me, remarkable image and perfectly matter-of-fact presentation. The door, for me, both echos the face and represents the dawning end of life. Wonderful image. For me, the chopping of the arm is in effect the counter-expression of the door; pieces are missing, the end is near, the exit awaits. It resonates with me because I juts lost my father exactly a year ago, and pieces of him were disappearing in some strange way as we watched.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-01-29 14:22:33.</i></td>', 'An 8 from me, remarkable image and perfectly matter-of-fact presentation. The door, for me, both echos the face and represents the dawning end of life. Wonderful image. For me, the chopping of the arm is in effect the counter-expression of the door; pieces are missing, the end is near, the exit awaits. It resonates with me because I juts lost my father exactly a year ago, and pieces of him were disappearing in some strange way as we watched.', '2010-01-29 14:20:50.000000', '2010-01-29 14:22:33.000000', 0),
(5843514, 847090, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bear_Music:</b></div><hr/><i> Might have expected this to finish higher, personally, but that ain''t bad for a man in a road in the desert, eh? Love the shot, gave it an 8. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>top 50 in this challenge?! no, not bad at all! Thanks Robert!</td>', 'Originally posted by Bear_Music: Might have expected this to finish higher, personally, but that ain''t bad for a man in a road in the desert, eh? Love the shot, gave it an 8.   top 50 in this challenge?! no, not bad at all! Thanks Robert!', '2010-01-29 14:23:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5843515, 848474, 30861, '<td valign="top">I''ll echo that, "seriously good". Got an 8 from me, and made me come back for several looks during the week. What particularly struck me is, which is the surface and which the ground, which is the wave and which is the substrate? I love ambiguity, I find it more and more in the simplest things as I age, though I''ve yet to find the courage (?) to attempt to render it.</td>', 'I''ll echo that, "seriously good". Got an 8 from me, and made me come back for several looks during the week. What particularly struck me is, which is the surface and which the ground, which is the wave and which is the substrate? I love ambiguity, I find it more and more in the simplest things as I age, though I''ve yet to find the courage (?) to attempt to render it.', '2010-01-29 14:25:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5843529, 847093, 52549, '<td valign="top">Very beautiful. Congratulations.</td>', 'Very beautiful. Congratulations.', '2010-01-29 14:44:21.000000', NULL, 0),
