(5843621, 848527, 38162, '<td valign="top">post comment:<br/>title refers to that one beat after the end of a nice solo stint that ended the piece; audience and musicians seemed to agree that he nailed it.  apologies for not getting the names as this was an early set at a club that treats jazz more as backdrop to the bar and dinner crowd - thus usually nyc session players, not "names" - I hope to print this and take it by the club and ask who they are and to give it to them.<br/> <br/>many thanks for your thoughtful comments!<br/>jim<br/> <br/></td>', 'post comment:title refers to that one beat after the end of a nice solo stint that ended the piece; audience and musicians seemed to agree that he nailed it.  apologies for not getting the names as this was an early set at a club that treats jazz more as backdrop to the bar and dinner crowd - thus usually nyc session players, not "names" - I hope to print this and take it by the club and ask who they are and to give it to them. many thanks for your thoughtful comments!jim ', '2010-01-29 16:01:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5843623, 847410, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by colorcarnival:</b></div><hr/><i> I was too busy looking at the wave flow that I did not notice the clouds.  They look cool.  Congrats on a great finish in the "best of"! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>did you notice the reflection of the rocks? That''s even more interesting. Great shot, Ben, Loved it in voting.</td>', 'Originally posted by colorcarnival: I was too busy looking at the wave flow that I did not notice the clouds.  They look cool.  Congrats on a great finish in the "best of"!   did you notice the reflection of the rocks? That''s even more interesting. Great shot, Ben, Loved it in voting.', '2010-01-29 16:02:37.000000', NULL, 0),
