(5844881, 847490, 27608, '<td valign="top">Great shot Brad!  I much prefer the BW over the colour version.  I love the amount of various shades present.</td>', 'Great shot Brad!  I much prefer the BW over the colour version.  I love the amount of various shades present.', '2010-01-30 21:03:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5844904, 848453, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b> GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB</b> <br/>Congratulations. You were there on one of those splendid treks to see the bears.  A friend went exploring on one of those treks in that area a summer ago and came back with wonderful images.  As, undoubtedly, did you.  I have the feeling that you have many more splendid images of bears from this shoot. <br/> <br/>These are awesome creatures, and it is no wonder that you wanted the image that was ''up close and personal.''  <br/> <br/>As far as a critique goes, this beautiful bear could have certainly used more space in the frame to show off its power.  <br/> <br/>I look forward to seeing more images from you at DPC.<br/> <br/>SFAlice<br/></td>', ' GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB Congratulations. You were there on one of those splendid treks to see the bears.  A friend went exploring on one of those treks in that area a summer ago and came back with wonderful images.  As, undoubtedly, did you.  I have the feeling that you have many more splendid images of bears from this shoot.  These are awesome creatures, and it is no wonder that you wanted the image that was ''up close and personal.''   As far as a critique goes, this beautiful bear could have certainly used more space in the frame to show off its power.   I look forward to seeing more images from you at DPC. SFAlice', '2010-01-30 21:22:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5844927, 848788, 15832, '<td valign="top">Ekki amalegt að ná þessum ribbon :)<br/> <br/>Congrats! Stunning photo...</td>', 'Ekki amalegt að ná þessum ribbon :) Congrats! Stunning photo...', '2010-01-30 21:33:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5844938, 848709, 18799, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>Boy, this is a really nice picture, tough to find constructive critiques. Keep in mind my comments are all merely suggestions and musings from my point of view. <br/> <br/>I love the expression on her face!  Who couldn''t have happy feelings looking at this?  The exposure is right on the money and the colors really pop.<br/> <br/>I feel slightly disconnected from her and think it''s because she is looking away.  I think if she had the same expression but was looking at the camera, this would have scored a full point higher.  Speaking of her eyes, they are really sharp, almost unnaturally so.  To me, perhaps a bit over done probably because they contrast so much with the softened skin.  I would have liked to have seen the crop a little different regarding the hands.  In general, it is not good to bisect a joint or to cut off fingers and I think that hurts the image a little.  Just a minor nit, since this is advanced editing, I think I would have toned down the bright spot above her head.  You might have even cropped a little tighter on top.<br/> <br/>Overall, I like this image and probably would have given it a 6 to 7 had I voted in the challenge.<br/> <br/>Hopefully these comments are somewhat helpful to you.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... Boy, this is a really nice picture, tough to find constructive critiques. Keep in mind my comments are all merely suggestions and musings from my point of view.  I love the expression on her face!  Who couldn''t have happy feelings looking at this?  The exposure is right on the money and the colors really pop. I feel slightly disconnected from her and think it''s because she is looking away.  I think if she had the same expression but was looking at the camera, this would have scored a full point higher.  Speaking of her eyes, they are really sharp, almost unnaturally so.  To me, perhaps a bit over done probably because they contrast so much with the softened skin.  I would have liked to have seen the crop a little different regarding the hands.  In general, it is not good to bisect a joint or to cut off fingers and I think that hurts the image a little.  Just a minor nit, since this is advanced editing, I think I would have toned down the bright spot above her head.  You might have even cropped a little tighter on top. Overall, I like this image and probably would have given it a 6 to 7 had I voted in the challenge. Hopefully these comments are somewhat helpful to you. ', '2010-01-30 21:39:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5844971, 848539, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I''d love to offer you a solid critique of what you could "do better to improve" this image, but I fear I cannot.  I love it just the way it is.  Marvelous composition and as I mentioned during the challenge, excellent DOF for this.  I suspect a handful may not have liked the processing - perhaps a bit too Topaz''ish/tonemapped for some - but I think it worked wonderfully!  You certainly paid a great deal of attention to detail with your processing to bring out the very best the picture had to offer - I applaud you for your vision and perserverence.  And while your other choice is very good, too, I like this one best.  Very nicely seen, captured and presented - definitely worthy of a "Best of" in my opinion.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! I''d love to offer you a solid critique of what you could "do better to improve" this image, but I fear I cannot.  I love it just the way it is.  Marvelous composition and as I mentioned during the challenge, excellent DOF for this.  I suspect a handful may not have liked the processing - perhaps a bit too Topaz''ish/tonemapped for some - but I think it worked wonderfully!  You certainly paid a great deal of attention to detail with your processing to bring out the very best the picture had to offer - I applaud you for your vision and perserverence.  And while your other choice is very good, too, I like this one best.  Very nicely seen, captured and presented - definitely worthy of a "Best of" in my opinion.', '2010-01-30 22:05:14.000000', NULL, 0),
