(5849036, 848474, 61961, '<td valign="top">I thought this was yours, Zeus, in light of some of your other recent challenge entries.  I know abstracts don''t please everyone but I''m a bit stymied by your super-low placement.  If I can be literal about the image, my first impression was "wave" -- though later I imagined a first-person view from the back of a bird in flight.  However, I''m sure you are more concerned with abstract qualities than "puzzle macro" images.<br/> <br/>This looks rather like a charcoal illustration, so my only qualm would be that one might think it was a photo of an existing artwork -- something I seem to remember being said about another "controversial" artwork of yours (and an impression I didn''t share, btw).<br/> <br/>I think it''s good for someone like me to know how to take the calendar-type images (before rejecting them), but I hope you keep doing what you are doing!</td>', 'I thought this was yours, Zeus, in light of some of your other recent challenge entries.  I know abstracts don''t please everyone but I''m a bit stymied by your super-low placement.  If I can be literal about the image, my first impression was "wave" -- though later I imagined a first-person view from the back of a bird in flight.  However, I''m sure you are more concerned with abstract qualities than "puzzle macro" images. This looks rather like a charcoal illustration, so my only qualm would be that one might think it was a photo of an existing artwork -- something I seem to remember being said about another "controversial" artwork of yours (and an impression I didn''t share, btw). I think it''s good for someone like me to know how to take the calendar-type images (before rejecting them), but I hope you keep doing what you are doing!', '2010-02-02 12:52:59.000000', NULL, 0),
